        "title": "Power Management - Sleep Modes, Clock Gating, Energy Budgets, Battery",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "For a battery or energy-harvested device, power is the dominant design\nconstraint — above clock speed, above RAM. A coin-cell sensor must run for\nyears on 225 mAh, which means the MCU spends >99% of its life asleep and wakes\nfor milliseconds. The entire discipline is: do the work fast, then *stop the\nclock and shut off everything you can*, and account for every microamp. Energy,\nnot speed, is the budget."
    }
